      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "The hypothesis claims that the observed phase transition in solution space rigidity (bifurcation in N_c(w)) is an artifact of fully-connected network inductive bias, and that switching to convolutional or spectral basis networks will eliminate it by enforcing translation invariance/smoothness priors. To test this, I need to explore the design space by running comparative experiments: (1) validate the baseline fully-connected network to establish the bifurcation, (2) implement convolutional/spectral variants, (3) measure N_c(w) trends for each architecture, and (4) statistically compare the results. This requires asynchronous hypothesis testing across multiple architectures to determine if the bifurcation persists or disappears."
    },
